  "stubs": [],
  "flags": [
    {
      "page": 1,
      "what": "This warband was read from its mordheimer.net page (https://mordheimer.net/docs/warbands/grade-2a-warbands/order-of-the-mare, last updated 12 Oct 2026), not from a PDF: https://www.broheim.net/downloads/warbands/web/Order%20Of%20The%20Mare.pdf answers 404. Every `page` below is 1, the page itself. See the decisions."
    },
    {
      "page": 1,
      "what": "The page's heroes are the Paragon (1), the Dame of the Mare (1), the Gallant (0-1) and the Esquiresses (0-2); its henchmen the Pilgrims (any number), the Bowmen (0-7), the Redeemed knights (0-5) and the Companion filly (0-1). No henchmen group sizes and no maximum profile are printed, so the warriors take our Human race."
    },
    {
      "page": 1,
      "what": "An Order of the Mare warband needs at least 3 models: our templates hold no minimum, so it is not imported."
    },
    {
      "page": 1,
      "what": "The page heads itself \"Grade: Heroic\" and \"Setting: Bretonnia / Mordheim\"; our warband type is grade 2a in Mordheim 2a, from mordheimer's own index, and is unchanged."
    },
    {
      "page": 1,
      "what": "The skill table has no Special column, so the warband has no skill group of its own. The Paragon and the Dame have no Shooting tick and the Esquiresses no Academic or Strength tick: as printed."
    },
    {
      "page": 1,
      "what": "\"Each warband must have one Paragon\" and \"must include a single Dame of the Mare\", so both are 1 exactly. That she is replaced without delay cannot be held as data, so it is the warband rule \"A Dame without delay\"."
    },
    {
      "page": 1,
      "what": "Knight's virtue is printed as a warband special rule that the Paragon, the Gallant and the Redeemed knights each point at, so it is their own rule and no warband rule: one special, on the three of them."
    },
    {
      "page": 1,
      "what": "The Lance line is \"(Knights only)\" and the Paragon's Vow of poverty forbids him a Lance, so the line is the Gallant's and the Redeemed knights'; his rule is kept so the player sees why. The other \"Knights only\" lines (Heavy armour, Barding, Warhorse) name all three."
    },
    {
      "page": 1,
      "what": "\"Weapons/Armour: Squires may be equipped from the Archer equipment list\" is the Esquiresses' line; the page calls them Squires there."
    },
    {
      "page": 1,
      "what": "The Paragon's Leader rule names \"the Questing knight\", which is the Paragon."
    },
    {
      "page": 1,
      "what": "Barding is 30 gc on this list where ours is 80 gc: the line price stands and ours is unchanged. Every other line matches our price (Warhorse 80, Horse 40, Longbow 15)."
    },
    {
      "page": 1,
      "what": "The Blessings of the Mare are a lore of six prayers, numbered 1 to 6 on the page. The Dame's rule calls them prayers, so she is a Priest. The Dame's charger (6) turns her into a warhorse-mounted model with the profile M8 WS4 BS0 S4 T4 W1 I4 A2 Ld7, which the prayer's own words carry; it is no mount of ours."
    },
    {
      "page": 1,
      "what": "\"Horse and rider\" halves the price of one horse or warhorse for the Paragon and the Gallant at recruitment. A conditional price cannot be held on a list line, so it stays a warband rule and the lines keep the full price."
    },
    {
      "page": 1,
      "what": "The page's \"A Word from the Author\", \"About Balance\" and lore sections are flavour and are not imported."
    }
  ]
}
